<title>UK: Croat Pliva buys 40,000 GDRs at $49.25.</title>
<headline>Croat Pliva buys 40,000 GDRs at $49.25.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Croatian pharmaceuticals company Pliva dd has repurchased 40,000 of its own global depositary receipts (GDRs) as part of plans to repurchase up to five percent of its stock.</p>
<p>The company said in a statement that the shares had been repurchased at $49.25 per GDR.</p>
<p>On 27 November, it bought back 20,000 GDRs at $49 per GDR.</p>
<p>Pliva's GDR issue, which was lead by Union Bank of Switzerland and Zagrebacka banka in March this year, was nearly 20 times oversubscribed and was priced at $18.71 per GDR.</p>
<p>The GDR was trading at $49.50/$50.50 by 1120 GMT in London.</p>
<p>-- David Chance London newsroom 44 171 542 5887</p>
</text>
